  "body": "Stacked on #3353 (merge #3353 first).\n\n## What changed\n\nBore takes the shared \"Pass starts at\" parameter of #3316. No new type.\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/bore.rs`: new entry `bore_started(p, pass_start)`. It orders the rings of each level with `PassStart::rank`. The old `bore(p)` calls it with Auto.\n  - Ring `k` (1 is the innermost ring, `count` is the wall ring) is the offset index `count - k` from the wall, in the outer family. A hole disk has no hole family.\n  - Auto: the centre-out walk. This is the old loop order, so Auto output does not change.\n  - Outside: the wall ring first, then each ring in to the centre.\n  - Inside: the rank law gives the centre-out order, because a hole has no inner wall. Inside is the same path as Auto.\n  - Each level still dives at the centre. The entry law (plunge, ramp along the radial sweep, the centre-cutting law) does not change.\n- `OpParams::Bore.pass_start`: the seed is Auto. `EditOperationParams` carries it with undo. The digest writes it only off Auto (the #3316 bytes).\n- Project key `pass_start` on the Bore DTO. `auto` is never written. No version step.\n- MCP: the generic `edit_operation` door. The #3316 patch guard finds the field by itself.\n- UI: the shared `Pass starts at` row on the Bore Passes tab, with a Bore hint (Inside is the centre-out order).\n- User guide: the Bore table row and one paragraph.\n- Decision file `docs/decisions/3360-bore-pass-start.md`. It leaves room for the #1448 start point and exit point.\n- Test fixtures: 13 `OpParams::Bore` literals get `pass_start: Auto`.\n\n## Cause\n\nBore had a fixed ring order (centre out). The maintainer asked that every kind with an order of passes or rings gets the shared option (#3316).\n\n## Hand trace, one level\n\nØ20 hole, Ø6 cutter, rc = 7, 3 rings (rho 2.33, 4.67, 7.0), kmax = 2:\n- Auto: ranks 0, 1, 2 for k = 1, 2, 3. Order 2.33, 4.67, 7.0 (as before).\n- Outside: ranks 2, 1, 0. Order 7.0, 4.67, 2.33. The sweep goes from the centre to the wall ring start, then each chord goes in by one ring.\n- Inside: ranks 3, 4, 5. Order 2.33, 4.67, 7.0.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n- `camcraft-motion` `bore_pass_start`:\n  - `bore_outside_starts_each_level_on_the_wall_and_walks_in`. Red on the stub that ignored the value: `Outside cuts the wall ring first: [2.33, 4.67, 7.0]`.\n  - `bore_auto_keeps_the_centre_out_ladder_byte_for_byte` (`bore` equals `bore_started(Auto)`, move for move).\n  - `bore_inside_is_the_centre_out_order`.\n- `camcraft-app` `bore_pass_start`:\n  - `bore_outside_cuts_the_wall_ring_first_through_generate`.\n  - `bore_pass_start_is_undoable_and_rides_the_project_file`.\n  - `mcp_sets_bore_pass_start_refuses_an_unknown_word_and_undo_restores_it`.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib `egui_app::tests::pass_start::the_bore_passes_tab_offers_pass_start_and_shows_the_draft`, and the Bore row in `every_field_lives_on_exactly_one_section`.\n\nMutations:\n- The ring sort disabled in `bore.rs`: the motion pin goes red. Restored: green.\n- The Bore arm of generate passes Auto instead of the op value: the app pin goes red. Restored: green.\n\nRuns on the final head (debug, without sccache):\n- motion: lib 533 ok; `bore_pass_start` 3; `bore_ramp_angle` 2; `bore_carried_ramp` 2; `machining2d` 68; `center_cut_law` 7; `level_links` 13; `top_z_level` 12; `refusal_ghost` 5; `equal_steps` 13; `entry_ramp_angle` 3. All ok.\n- app: lib 297 ok; `bore_pass_start` 3; `bore_entry` 4; `bore_core` 6; `break_through` 12; `coarse_rims` 5; `conformance` 7; `golden_cl` 33; `hole_wall_flats` 5; `ladder_entry_height` 5; `lathe_workholding_kinds` 10 (1 ignored); `mcp_enum_patch` 3; `mill2d_c` 9; `offset_pass_start` 3; `project_roundtrip` 76; `refusal_location` 3; `setup_align_hole_kinds` 4; `stepped_stock_rapid` 8; `stock_source_holes` 9; `stock_source_verdict` 22; `thread_mill_rim` 13. All ok.\n- ui: lib 1425 ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Gate\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` did not complete. The diff against `upstream/main` includes all of #3353, so the plan had several hundred app binaries. All 82 motion steps passed. Then the app build step did not finish within the 2-hour background limit: the shared sccache server stalled while other workers built. The runs above replace it, without sccache. The full quick gate is **not run** on this head.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `golden_cl` (33) and `conformance` (7) pass with no golden change.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Heavy lanes: not run.\n- Outside with a through hole, with stock to leave and with several holes is not pinned. The ring order code is the same for each hole.\n- Outside makes the wall ring a full slot in solid stock, and the wall is cut before the inner rings. This is what the option asks for. Auto stays the default.\n- No GUI screenshot.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill row for Bore is not added: the edit of `.claude/skills/` needed an approval in this session. The #3316 row already names the key.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3353: the parent. This PR adds Bore beside 2D Offset in the same files (`pass_start_row.rs`, `params.rs`, `params_impl.rs`, `generate.rs`, `mill2d` digest). Merge #3353 first.\n- #3387 (Face, also stacked on #3353) touches `pass_start_row.rs`, `generate.rs`, `params.rs`: different functions. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #3103 (Bore Helical strategy, `needs-rework`) touches `bore.rs` (`BoreParams`, `validate`) and the Bore params: different functions. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Bore: new \"Pass starts at\" option (Auto / Inside / Outside) on the Passes tab. Outside cuts each level's wall ring first and works in to the centre. Auto and Inside keep the centre-out order.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3360\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
